                    '   and were granted shares worth $110K and options over shares worth $300K at the time. Over the same years those companies produced -$483.0M of owner cash.', \
                    '   At 2 of the 2, insiders sold more than the business produced for its owners; among the cash-generative companies it was 1 of 1.' \
                ], \
                '', \
                '**What it costs a shareholder.** Each share owns a smaller part of a company that produces no cash for its owners, at a', \
