# A company's page with one insider's filings
async function testMain_companyPerson():
    data = testData(['data/meta.json', 'data/company/1.json'])
    systemGlobalSet('vPage', 'company')
    systemGlobalSet('vCik', 1)
    systemGlobalSet('vPerson', 1001)
    unittestMockAll(data)
    tiMain()
    log = unittestMockEnd()
    systemGlobalSet('vPage', null)
    systemGlobalSet('vCik', null)
    systemGlobalSet('vPerson', null)
    unittestDeepEqual(log, [ \
        [ \
            'systemFetch', \
            [ \
                ['data/meta.json', 'data/company/1.json'] \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '[Index](#var=&_top) | [Group totals](#var.vPage=\'totals\'&_top) | [Threshold explorer](#var.vPage=\'explore\'&_top) | [Methodology](#var.vPage=\'method\'&_top) | [Data and limits](#var.vPage=\'data\'&_top) | [Downloads](#var.vPage=\'downloads\'&_top)' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'documentSetTitle', \
            ['Stock Pay Co - The Treadmill Index'] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '# Stock Pay Co', \
                '', \
                '**Ticker:** SPAY (Nasdaq) \\\n**SEC filings:** [CIK 1](https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=1&type=10-K) \\\n**Industry:** Services\\-Prepackaged Software ([SIC 7372](#var.vSic=7372&var.vType=\'all\'&_top)) \\\n**Type:** Stock pay. Passed the screen: owner cash is under the line and stock pay is the cause.', \
                '', \
                'From fiscal 2019 to 2025, Stock Pay Co reported $10.2 billion of revenue and $1.0 billion of free cash flow. Stock pay was $1.2 billion, which leaves -$203 million of owner cash: -2.0% of revenue. Owner cash was under 3.0% of revenue in 7 of 7 years. In the 12 months to 2026-09-30 it was -2.0% of revenue.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '## Which way the numbers point', \
                '', \
                [ \
                    '| Sign | A growth bet paying off | A treadmill | This company |', \
                    '| :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- |', \
                    '| Owner cash as the company grows | Appears | Stays near zero | Under 3.0% of revenue in 7 of 7 years, and for the latest 7 running. -2.0% in the latest 12 months. |', \
                    '| Operating costs against revenue, over five years | Fall, and leave part of gross profit | Keep pace or rise, and take all of gross profit | 55.0% of revenue in 2021, 55.0% in 2025, when they took 91.7% of gross profit; sales and marketing 32.0% to 28.0% |', \
                    '| Insiders, 2021‑2025 | Keep what they are granted | Sell it | Sold $110K; granted stock worth $110K and options over shares worth $300K: between 0.3x and 1.0x what they were granted |', \
                    '| Owner cash against insider sales, 2021‑2025 | Owners get more than insiders take out | Insiders take out more | Owner cash -$161.0M; insider sales $110K |', \
                    '| Share count, 2021‑2025 | Falls when the company buys back shares | Holds or rises despite buybacks | Rose 2.0% a year, after $40.0M of buybacks and employees\' vesting taxes |' \
                ] \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            ['', '## What cuts the other way', ''] \
